    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered sequence of validations and side-effects when you `POST /api/owners`. I've grouped them by the pipeline stage they occur in, since order matters across layers.\n\n## Stage 0 \u2014 Before the controller runs\n\n1. **Idempotency filter** (`IdempotentCreateFilter`): if the request carries an `Idempotency-Key` header that was seen before, the stored prior response is **replayed as `200 OK`** and the controller never runs. Otherwise the request proceeds and a successful (2xx) response is cached under that key.\n2. **Authorization** (`@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`): caller must have `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` (when method security is enabled). Failure \u2192 `403`.\n\n## Stage 1 \u2014 Bean Validation on the request body (`@Valid OwnerFieldsDto`)\n\nApplied before any controller code; any failure \u2192 `400` with a `schemaValidationErrors` list (via `ExceptionControllerAdvice`).\n\n3. `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words with space/'/-).\n4. `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (like firstName, optional trailing `.`).\n5. `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2` \u2014 each `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern` (must contain a non-blank char).\n6. `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern` (non-blank).\n7. `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, `@Pattern` (phone shape), plus custom `@E164NationalLength` (national-digit count must match country code, e.g. `+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210).\n8. `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`, plus custom `@NonDisposableEmail` (rejects `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`).\n9. `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^\\d{4}$)`.\n10. `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 `@PastOrPresent`.\n11. `title` \u2014 `@Size(1..10)`.\n12. **Class-level `@ValidPostcode`** \u2014 cross-field: the 4-digit postcode must fall in the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Blank postcode or unknown region passes.\n\n## Stage 2 \u2014 Mapping DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity (`OwnerMapper.toOwner`)\n\nThese are normalization side-effects that run inside the entity's setters as the mapper populates it:\n\n13. **Email lowercased** (`setEmail`).\n14. **Telephone normalized to E.164** via `PhoneNumbers.toE164` (`setTelephone`).\n15. **Address normalized** via `AddressNormalizer.normalize` and recomposed (`setAddress`/`setAddressLine1`/`setAddressLine2`).\n\n## Stage 3 \u2014 Controller business logic (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`), in order\n\n16. **`registrationDate` rolled forward to a business day** via `BusinessDay.adjust` (skips weekends and hardcoded 2026 holidays); defaults to today if absent.\n17. Loads all non-deleted owners for the checks below.\n18. **Rate-limit check** \u2014 if \u2265 100 owners already share that registration date \u2192 return `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` (aborts, no save).\n19. **Identity / city-cap check** \u2014 if an existing owner has the same `identityKey` (telephone + email) **OR** \u2265 50 owners already exist in the same city \u2192 `409 CONFLICT` (aborts).\n20. **`namesakeCount` set** = number of existing owners with the same first + last name (case-insensitive).\n21. **Household-duplicate guard** \u2014 if any existing owner is in the same household (last name + postcode) and the request did **not** set `sharesHousehold=true` \u2192 `409 CONFLICT` (aborts).\n22. **`householdMemberCount` set** = 1 + existing owners in the same household.\n23. **`customerCode` computed** via `CustomerCode.of` (`<REGION>-<sha256 hash8>`, with `-n` suffix to dedup against existing codes).\n24. **`possibleDuplicate` set to `false`; `possibleDuplicateOf` set to `null`.**\n\n## Stage 4 \u2014 Persistence (`ClinicService.saveOwner` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save`)\n\nThe service is a thin `@Transactional` pass-through \u2014 no password encoding, no events, no email.\n\n25. **`@PrePersist` `defaultRegistrationDate`** \u2014 sets `registrationDate` to today if still null (defensive; controller already set it).\n26. **`save`** inserts the row.\n27. **`@PostPersist` `OwnerAuditListener.onCreate`** \u2014 writes an **audit log line** (`AUDIT` logger) with id, customerCode, registrationDate, computed membership level, and membership number.\n\n## Stage 5 \u2014 Response assembly\n\n28. Maps saved entity \u2192 `OwnerDto`.\n29. **`bulkSignupWarning` set to `true`** if > 80 owners share the registration date.\n30. Sets `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header and returns **`201 CREATED`**.\n\n## Notes on things that are *not* in this path\n- **No password encoding / no email sending / no event publishing** anywhere in owner creation (the `BCryptPasswordEncoder` exists only for user authentication).\n- A `DataIntegrityViolationException` at save time is mapped by the advice to **`404`** (not the more conventional 409) \u2014 worth flagging as unusual, though you asked only to read, not change.\n- The create endpoint is served by the **V1** controller; `OwnerRestControllerV2` only implements the GET list."
